/* ============ DATA: handwritten events ============
 fx language: r <res> n | g <sel> <attr> n | o <org> <attr> n | c <org> <eth> pts | m <sel> n p|t text
 v <rival> <attr> n | law <law> <opt> | reg <id> <attr> n | fed <id> 0|1 | x <special> args.  Leading ? = hidden tier.
 ch = chance branches [p, fx, text]; d = [minTurns, maxTurns, followUpId]; f = flag; fu = follow-up only. */
D.ev=[
/* ---- Chain 1: the Ford ---- */
{id:'ford',t:'The Killing at Stonewater Ford',era:[1],w:40,who:'Elder Brann of the Vale',
x:`Ordu, war-chief of the Hill Kaldar, has killed a Vale herder in a quarrel over summer grazing at Stonewater Ford. The Vale elders want him cast out. Ordu's kin wait armed on the far bank. He says the pasture was his grandfather's before any Vale plough touched it.`,
q:`"Shaman, the blood is on the stones. What is your judgment?"`,
ch:[{l:'Exile Ordu beyond the ford',fx:'g eth:kr loy 6; r ord 3; m eth:kh -14 p the exile of Ordu at Stonewater Ford',d:[5,10,'ford2'],f:'ford_exile'},
{l:'Set a blood-price in cattle',fx:'r food -4; g eth:kr loy 1; g eth:kh loy 3; r tra 3; r ord 2',ch:[[.3,'g eth:kr grv 8','The dead man\'s brothers call the price an insult.']]},
{l:'Swear a brotherhood oath: the pasture is shared',fx:'o noble loy -6; g eth:kr loy -4; m eth:kh 14 p the Ford Oath of shared pasture',d:[5,10,'ford2'],f:'ford_oath'}]},
{id:'ford2',t:'The Heir of Ordu',fu:1,who:'A Hill Kaldar rider',
x:`A rider who names Ordu as forebear, {kin} of that line, stands at the ford. {?ford_oath:Vale settlers have ploughed the shared pasture, and the Ford Oath you swore in your {srcOrd} life is being eaten furrow by furrow.|The line has raided from exile for years. Now it offers peace, if the pasture lost in your {srcOrd} life is returned.}`,
q:`"You remember the ford, they say. Then remember us. Whose grass is it?"`,
ch:[{l:'Give the pasture to the Hill clans',fx:'g eth:kh loy 8; g eth:kh grv -8; g eth:kr+cls:farmer grv 10; o noble loy -5'},
{l:'Refuse: the Vale keeps what it ploughs',fx:'g eth:kr loy 5; m eth:kh -16 p {?ford_oath:the breaking of the Ford Oath|the second refusal at the ford}',ch:[[.4,'reg hk unrest 15; r ord -5','Hill riders burn three Vale steadings.']]},
{l:'Raise a boundary stone and divide it',fx:'r tre -4; g eth:kh loy 3; g eth:kr loy -2',d:[5,10,'ford3'],f:'ford_stone'}]},
{id:'ford3',t:'The Ford Stone',fu:1,who:'Kelda, a Hill-born Keeper',
x:`The boundary stone at the ford has become a shrine. Hill Kaldar gather there each spring. Kelda, a Keeper born in High Kald, asks that the Hill clans have their own Circle, chanting in High Kaldic, answering to you but not to the Vale Keepers.`,
q:`"We believe in you. Must we also believe in them?"`,
ch:[{l:'Grant the Hill Circle',fx:'o priest loy -12; o priest pow -3; g eth:kh bel 12; g eth:kh loy 6; reg hk integ 6; c priest kh 15'},
{l:'One Circle, one chant',fx:'o priest loy 7; r tra 3; g eth:kh bel -6; g eth:kh grv 5'},
{l:'Seat Kelda in the Vale Circle instead',fx:'c priest kh 8; g eth:kh loy 4; o priest loy -2; r ord 2',ch:[[.25,'g eth:kh grv 6','The Vale Keepers freeze her out. The Hill clans notice.']]}]},
/* ---- Chain 2: the Keepers ---- */
{id:'keeper1',t:'Mother Senna\'s Chant',era:[1],w:30,who:'Mother Senna, eldest of your followers',
x:`Mother Senna has followed you since before the others believed. She asks leave to fix your sayings into a chant that only her Circle may teach, word for word, so that nothing is lost when this body is.`,
q:`"When you are gone, who will know what you meant? Let it be us."`,
ch:[{l:'Let the Circle keep the chant',fx:'o priest pow 6; o priest aut 8; r tra 4; g rel:ret_s bel -3',d:[5,10,'keeper2'],f:'chant_fixed'},
{l:'Teach it openly to anyone who asks',fx:'r cha 5; g all bel 3; o priest loy -8',d:[5,10,'keeper2']},
{l:'Forbid fixing the words at all',fx:'r cha 6; o priest aut -6; o priest loy -4; ?o priest dev -6',pv:'What is not written can be remembered many ways.'}]},
{id:'keeper2',t:'The Rule and the Mouth',fu:1,who:'A young Keeper, respectfully',
x:`The Circle now teaches "Senna's Rule", begun in your {srcOrd} life. Yesterday you said something that contradicts it. A young Keeper kneels and asks, before the whole court, which is true: the Rule, or your mouth.`,
q:`"If you can err, what are we keeping? If the Rule can err, what are you?"`,
ch:[{l:'"My mouth. The Rule is a memory of me."',fx:'r cha 6; o priest loy -10; o priest aut -8; r leg -3'},
{l:'"The Rule binds even me."',fx:'r leg 5; r tra 3; o priest aut 10; o priest loy 6; r cha -6',d:[5,10,'keeper3']},
{l:'Convene a synod to amend the Rule',fx:'r tre -4; o priest dev 8; o priest loy 4; r leg 2',d:[5,10,'keeper3']}]},
{id:'keeper3',t:'The Steward of the Empty Seat',fu:1,who:'The synod of Keepers',
x:`The synod proposes an office: between your lives a Steward of the Empty Seat will hold your authority, chosen by the Keepers from among themselves. It would end the hungry years after each death. It would also give someone a reason to prefer the seat empty.`,
q:`"Will you bless the Stewardship?"`,
ch:[{l:'Bless it',fx:'o priest pow 8; o priest aut 12; r tra 4; r ord 3',f:'steward'},
{l:'The seat stays empty until I fill it',fx:'r cha 4; o priest loy -8; ?o priest dev -5'},
{l:'Let the council elect the Steward',fx:'o council pow 8; o council aut 6; o priest loy -10; r leg 4',f:'steward_council'}]},
/* ---- Chain 3: the Search ---- */
{id:'search1',t:'The Office of the Search',era:[2,3],w:14,c:{min:{lives:2}},who:'Brother Edrin, who found you',
x:`Brother Edrin walked four winters to find this body. He asks that the Search be made a sacred office with its own lands, so that the next finding does not depend on one stubborn man's feet.`,
q:`"I found you by luck and blisters. Shall the next finder have more?"`,
ch:[{l:'Endow the Search with lands',fx:'r tre -8; o priest pow 5; o priest aut 8; x recog 8',d:[5,10,'search2']},
{l:'Keep the Search a calling, not an office',fx:'o priest loy -3; r cha 2'},
{l:'Give the council a seat on the Search',fx:'o council pow 5; o priest loy -6; r leg 3',d:[5,10,'search2']}]},
{id:'search2',t:'The Child They Passed Over',fu:1,adv:1,who:'An anonymous letter',
x:`A letter claims that in the last Search a child in a far village knew every sign, and was passed over because the family was not Kaldar. The Searchers call it slander. If it is true, the Search finds who it wishes to find.`,
q:`"Will you look into it?"`,
ch:[{l:'Open inquiry before the court',fx:'o priest loy -8; r leg 3',ch:[[.5,'o priest aut -10; g all bel 4; x recog 6','The letter was true. Two Searchers are dismissed.'],[.5,'o priest loy -4','Nothing is proven. The Searchers do not forgive the doubt.']],d:[5,10,'search3']},
{l:'Quiet inquiry through a trusted clerk',fx:'r tre -4',ch:[[.4,'o priest aut -5; x recog 4','The clerk confirms it. You correct the Searchers privately.']],d:[5,10,'search3']},
{l:'Let it lie',fx:'o priest loy 3; ?x claim 5; ?g all bel -2',pv:'The Searchers will know you did not look.'}]},
{id:'search3',t:'The Golden Bowl',fu:1,who:'An envoy of the Imeric Crown',
x:`The Imeric Crown, citing "disputes" over your returns, offers a gift: a golden bowl from which the name of the true Returner shall be drawn by lot, under the eyes of its envoys, for the peace of all neighbours.`,
q:`"Surely the true soul has nothing to fear from an honest bowl?"`,
ch:[{l:'Accept the bowl and the envoys',fx:'v crown att 15; law recog urn; o priest loy -8; ?x claim 10',f:'crown_bowl',pv:'Whoever watches the lots may one day hold them.'},
{l:'Make our own urn, under the council',fx:'law recog urn; o council pow 5; v crown att -6; o priest loy -6'},
{l:'"Only memory proves me." Trial of Memory',fx:'law recog trial; r cha 5; v crown att -8; o priest loy -6'},
{l:'Refuse. The Keepers search as before',fx:'v crown att -10; o priest loy 6'}]},
/* ---- Chain 4: the Scribes ---- */
{id:'scribe1',t:'The Tongue of the Tallies',era:[1,2],w:22,c:{tech:['writing']},who:'The chief scribe',
x:`The tallies have outgrown memory. The chief scribe asks in which tongue they shall be kept. One tongue is cheap and makes one people the gatekeepers. Many tongues are fair and slow.`,
q:`"A tally is a small thing. But whoever reads it reads the realm."`,
ch:[{l:'Kaldic only',fx:'law lang kaldic',d:[5,10,'scribe2']},
{l:'Each land keeps its own',fx:'law lang custom; r tre -3'},
{l:'Many tongues, with sworn interpreters',fx:'law lang multi'}]},
{id:'scribe2',t:'Davit\'s Examination',fu:1,who:'A trader, father of the boy',
x:`Davit, a trader's son, the best reckoner of his year, has failed the scribes' examination. His sums were perfect. His Kaldic was not. His father has paid for a petition and stands holding it as if it were hot.`,
q:`"He can count your whole realm. Must he also sound like you?"`,
ch:[{l:'Admit him as an exception',fx:'r tre -2; o council loy -3; o merch loy 4'},
{l:'Open the examinations to other tongues',fx:'law lang multi; o council loy -8; g core loy -3'},
{l:'Uphold the examiners',fx:'o council loy 5; g cls:merchant grv 6',d:[5,10,'scribe3'],pv:'Clever people shut out of one door build another.'}]},
{id:'scribe3',t:'The Mother-Tongue School',fu:1,who:'The council\'s censor',
x:`The line of Davit, now led by his {kin}, runs a school that teaches reckoning in the mother tongue and copies a grammar of it. Half the merchants' children attend. The council's censor calls it a second chancery in waiting.`,
q:`"Close it now, or explain to your grandchildren why you did not."`,
ch:[{l:'Close the school',fx:'o council loy 8; r ord 3; r leg 2; g lang:kal loy 3; g cls:merchant grv 8; m cls:merchant -10 p the closing of the mother-tongue school; ?g all grv 2'},
{l:'Charter it under the realm',fx:'o council loy -10; g lang:kal loy -3; r kno 3; g cls:merchant loy 5; o merch loy 4; ?x cohere 1'},
{l:'Fund a rival school in both tongues',fx:'r tre -7; r kno 6; g cls:merchant loy 3; o council loy -2'}]},
/* ---- Chain 5: the Vek riders ---- */
{id:'vek1',t:'Tabar\'s Three Hundred',era:[1,2],w:22,who:'Tabar, a Sorvek war-leader',
x:`Tabar lost a quarrel with his khan and arrives with three hundred riders, their families and no country. He offers their bows for pasture on the edge of High Kald. The Hill clans graze there now.`,
q:`"A khan feeds his riders or loses them. Will you be our khan?"`,
ch:[{l:'Settle them as your household guard',fx:'o army pow 10; c army sv 25; g eth:kh grv 8; v horde att -6; x addpop hk sv vek sky warrior 5',d:[5,10,'vek2'],f:'vek_guard'},
{l:'Hire them for one season',fx:'r tre -6; o army pow 6; r ord 3',ch:[[.25,'r food -5','Unpaid at season\'s end, they take cattle on the way out.']]},
{l:'Turn them away',fx:'v horde att 5; g eth:kh loy 3',ch:[[.4,'r food -6; reg hk unrest 8','Hungry riders take what was not offered.']]}]},
{id:'vek2',t:'Who Holds the Gate',fu:1,who:'The Kaldar captains',
x:`Tabar's {kin} commands the guard. Vek riders hold the gate, the granary and your bedchamber door. The Kaldar captains say plainly that a ruler guarded by strangers is ruled by them.`,
q:`"We bled for this seat before they could find it on a map. Choose."`,
ch:[{l:'Dismiss the Vek guard',fx:'o army pow -8; c army kr 20; g eth:kr loy 4',ch:[[.35,'r ord -10; r tre -6','The riders do not leave quietly.']]},
{l:'Raise a Kaldar regiment beside them',fx:'r tre -10; o army pow 5; c army kr 10',d:[5,10,'vek3']},
{l:'Make their commander marshal of all',fx:'o army loy 6; c army sv 15; g eth:kr+cls:warrior grv 12',d:[5,10,'vek3']}]},
{id:'vek3',t:'The Khan\'s Kin',fu:1,who:'A herald of the Sorvek Horde',
x:`The Horde's khan sends a herald. The riders in your guard are Sorvek, he says, and Sorvek have one protector under the sky. He asks to be named so in your court, with the right to hear their complaints.`,
q:`"They guard your door. Who guards them?"`,
ch:[{l:'Name the khan their protector',fx:'v horde att 15; o army loy -8; r leg -3; ?o army dev -10'},
{l:'Refuse and raise their pay',fx:'r tre -8; o army loy 5; v horde att -8'},
{l:'Offer the riders the oath of belonging',fx:'law cit oath; v horde att -5; g eth:sv loy 8; g core loy -5; o noble loy -4',pv:'Changes the law of belonging for everyone.'}]},
/* ---- Chain 6: House Mare ---- */
{id:'mare1',t:'Salt and Silver',era:[1,2],w:22,who:'Ila Mare, a Soranni trader',
x:`Ila Mare of Reedmouth lays a bar of silver on your mat. She wants the sole right to bring salt up the river. Your herders will pay more for salt. Your treasury will, for once, have something in it.`,
q:`"Everyone buys salt. Why should everyone sell it?"`,
ch:[{l:'Grant the salt right',fx:'r tre 14; o merch pow 6; g cls:herder grv 6; g cls:farmer grv 4; m eth:so 8 p the salt grant to House Mare',d:[5,10,'mare2'],f:'mare_grant'},
{l:'Open market, with a toll at the ford',fx:'r tre 5; v league att 4'},
{l:'Salt is for Kaldar to trade',fx:'g eth:kr loy 3; v league att -6; o merch loy -4'}]},
{id:'mare2',t:'The Debt to House Mare',fu:1,who:'The head of House Mare',
x:`House Mare has lent to your treasury since the salt grant of your {srcOrd} life. The head of the house, Ila's {kin}, proposes to forgive the debt in exchange for the right to collect the taxes of one land and keep a tenth.`,
q:`"You dislike collecting. We are good at it."`,
ch:[{l:'Farm the taxes to House Mare',fx:'r tre 10; o merch pow 8; o merch aut 8; g cls:farmer grv 8; o council loy -6',d:[5,10,'mare3']},
{l:'Repay in full',fx:'r tre -14; o merch loy 4'},
{l:'Repudiate the debt',fx:'o merch loy -15; v league att -12; m eth:so -10 t the repudiated debt; g cls:farmer loy 3'}]},
{id:'mare3',t:'Credit Wants Continuity',fu:1,who:'House Mare\'s banker',
x:`House Mare now holds enough paper to make or break a harvest. Its banker asks, pleasantly, for a seat among those who recognize your return. Lenders, he says, lend at better rates when they know who will be sitting in the seat next time.`,
q:`"We ask only to be in the room."`,
ch:[{l:'Give them the seat',fx:'r tre 10; o merch pow 6; o merch aut 8; o priest loy -6; ?x claim 6'},
{l:'Refuse, and tax their paper',fx:'r tre 6; o merch loy -12; v league att -6'},
{l:'Refuse, but borrow elsewhere',fx:'r tre -6; o merch loy -4; v league att 4'}]},
/* ---- Chain 7: land ---- */
{id:'land1',t:'Haldric\'s Fences',era:[1,2],w:18,who:'Haldric, clan head',
x:`Haldric wants to fence the common meadow of his valley and plant it in barley for the war band. More grain, he says, and he will answer for it. The families who graze there will answer to him.`,
q:`"The commons feeds everyone a little. I can feed your spears a great deal."`,
ch:[{l:'Let the clan heads enclose',fx:'law land estates',d:[5,10,'land2']},
{l:'The commons stay common',fx:'o noble loy -6; g cls:farmer loy 4'},
{l:'Divide it as freeholds for veterans',fx:'law land free; o army loy 6'}]},
{id:'land2',t:'Sanctuary',fu:1,who:'The Keeper of the shrine',
x:`Forty bonded labourers have fled the estate of Haldric's {kin} and sit in the shrine court holding its doorposts. They say you once said no one who holds your threshold may be taken. No one can find where you said it. The estate's riders are at the gate.`,
q:`"Did you say it? Will you say it now?"`,
ch:[{l:'"I said it." Shelter them',fx:'o noble loy -10; g cls:bonded bel 12; g cls:bonded loy 8; o priest pow 3',d:[5,10,'land3'],f:'sanctuary'},
{l:'Return them to the estate',fx:'o noble loy 6; g cls:bonded grv 12; m cls:bonded -10 p the forty returned from the shrine'},
{l:'Buy their bonds from the treasury',fx:'r tre -10; o noble loy -2; g cls:bonded loy 6'}]},
{id:'land3',t:'The Threshold March',fu:1,who:'A woman at the head of the march',
x:`The landless have made your sanctuary saying into a movement. Thousands walk toward the capital carrying doorposts. They do not threaten. They ask you to walk at their head to the estates and repeat the words there.`,
q:`"You said it in your {srcOrd} life. Say it where the fences are."`,
ch:[{l:'Walk at their head',fx:'r cha 10; g cls:bonded loy 12; g cls:farmer loy 8; o noble loy -18; o army loy -5',ch:[[.3,'r ord -10','Two great houses arm their tenants.']]},
{l:'Answer with a land law, not a march',fx:'law land free; r leg 4; g cls:farmer loy 4'},
{l:'Disperse the march',fx:'r ord 4; o noble loy 8; g cls:bonded grv 14; m cls:bonded -14 p the breaking of the Threshold March; r cha -6'}]},
/* ---- Chain 8: the burned shrine ---- */
{id:'salt1',t:'The Tithe Refused',era:[1,2,3],w:16,pick:'newReg',who:'Your war-captain',
x:`In {rn} the old priests of the {gn} have barred your Keepers from the granaries and refused the tithe. Your captain says one burned shrine now will save ten risings later. The priests say they will pay a tax to a ruler, never a tithe to a god who is not theirs.`,
q:`"Give the word and it is done by morning. What is the word?"`,
ch:[{l:'Burn the shrine',fx:'r ord 6; g $g fear 40; reg $r unrest -10; m $g -22 p the burning of the shrine in {rn}; v crown att -10',d:[5,10,'salt2'],f:'burned'},
{l:'Call it a tax, not a tithe',fx:'r tre 3; o priest loy -11; g $g loy 4',d:[6,11,'salt3']},
{l:'Expel the priests, spare the shrine',fx:'g $g grv 6; reg $r unrest 4; o priest loy 6; r ord 3'}]},
{id:'salt2',t:'The Lament',fu:1,who:'Your steward',
x:`A lament for the shrine burned in {rn} in your {srcOrd} life is sung at every {gn} wedding. It names no one. Everyone knows who it means. Your steward asks whether singers should be arrested, or whether you would prefer to attend the yearly mourning yourself.`,
q:`"It is only a song. That is what worries me."`,
ch:[{l:'Ban the lament',fx:'g $g fear 25; g $g grv 5; r ord 4; o army loy 3; ?m $g -8 t the banned lament'},
{l:'Attend the mourning and atone',fx:'r cha -4; g $g loy 7; m $g 8 t the atonement at {rn}; o army loy -6; o priest loy -6',d:[5,10,'salt3']},
{l:'Let them sing',fx:'g $g loy 2'}]},
{id:'salt3',t:'A Realm Within the Realm',fu:1,who:'An envoy of the Imeric Crown',
x:`{?burned:The Imeric Crown has taken up the burned shrine of {rn} as its own wound.|The untithed shrines of {rn} have grown rich and answer to no one.} An envoy asks that the Crown be named guardian of the old rites among the {gn}, with the right to appoint their priests.`,
q:`"You need not love them. Let us do it for you."`,
ch:[{l:'Name the Crown guardian',fx:'v crown att 18; g $g loy 4; r leg -5; reg $r integ -12; ?x claim 6'},
{l:'Appoint their priests yourself',fx:'g $g grv 6; o priest loy -4; reg $r integ 6; v crown att -8'},
{l:'Let the {gn} elect their own',fx:'g $g loy 8; v crown att -4; o priest loy -6; fed $r 1'}]},
/* ---- Chain 9: prophecy ---- */
{id:'proph1',t:'Where Will You Be Born?',era:[1,2],w:20,who:'Vessa, a dying follower',
x:`Vessa followed you for thirty years and is dying before you. She has one question and wants an answer she can carry. Everyone in the room is listening, and whatever you say will be repeated long after anyone can ask what you meant.`,
q:`"Where will you be born next? Among whom shall we look?"`,
ch:[{l:'"Among the lowest."',fx:'g cls:bonded bel 12; g cls:farmer bel 5; o noble loy -6',d:[5,10,'proph2'],f:'proph_low'},
{l:'"Among my own, in the Vale."',fx:'g eth:kr bel 6; g eth:kr loy 4; g eth:kh bel -4',d:[5,10,'proph2'],f:'proph_vale'},
{l:'"Where I am needed. Do not ask."',fx:'r cha 7; g all bel 2; o priest loy -2'}]},
{id:'proph2',t:'The Prophecy Weighed',fu:1,who:'A Keeper with a scroll',
x:`The Keepers have found Vessa's question in the records of your {srcOrd} life. You answered: {?proph_low:"Among the lowest."|"Among my own, in the Vale."} You were born this time among the {be}, to a family of {bc}. The Keeper asks how the court should understand this.`,
q:`"Were you wrong then, or are you not who you say now?"`,
ch:[{l:'"The words meant more than you heard."',fx:'r cha 3; o priest loy -4; g all bel -2',d:[5,10,'proph3']},
{l:'"I was wrong. Souls do not choose."',fx:'r cha -5; r leg 3; g all bel -3; o priest dev -4'},
{l:'Have the record corrected',fx:'o priest aut 6; o council loy -3; ?x claim 5',pv:'Those who edit your past for you can edit it without you.'}]},
{id:'proph3',t:'The Returner in Every Child',fu:1,who:'A Seeker preacher',
x:`A Seeker teaching spreads: your prophecy meant that the Returner is born in every child, a little. No Search is needed, and no seat. The poor love it. The Keepers want it condemned today.`,
q:`"If you are in all of us, why do they keep you in one room?"`,
ch:[{l:'Embrace the teaching',fx:'g rel:ret_s bel 10; g all bel 5; g all loy 3; o priest loy -15; o priest pow -6; ?x claim 8',f:'universal'},
{l:'Condemn it',fx:'o priest loy 8; g rel:ret_s grv 12; m rel:ret_s -10 t the condemnation of the Seekers'},
{l:'Permit it as a lay devotion',fx:'o priest loy -5; g rel:ret_s loy 5'}]},
/* ---- Chain 10: the spare claimant ---- */
{id:'claim1',t:'The Spare',era:[2,3,4],w:14,c:{min:{lives:2}},who:'An old Keeper, uneasy',
x:`Before you were found, the {ctrl} had prepared another child, in case. His name is Pell. He was taught your gestures and your chant. He is your age now, lives in a cell at the mountain shrine, and has never been told he is not you.`,
q:`"We did not know what to do with him. We still do not."`,
ch:[{l:'Bring Pell to court as a brother',fx:'r cha 3; o priest loy 3; x claim 5',d:[5,10,'claim2'],f:'pell_court'},
{l:'Send him far away with a pension',fx:'r tre -4; x claim -4',d:[6,11,'claim2']},
{l:'See that he is never heard of again',fx:'x claim -10; o priest dev -6; ?m rel:ret_s -8 p the silencing of Pell',pv:'Someone always tells.'}]},
{id:'claim2',t:'The Pellites',fu:1,who:'A delegation in grey',
x:`{?pell_court:Pell was gentle at court and people noticed.|Pell preached in exile and people listened.} His followers, who dress in grey, say the soul can be poured into two cups. They do not deny you. They ask only that Pell's line also be searched for when he dies.`,
q:`"Two lamps give more light. Why would the Returner mind?"`,
ch:[{l:'Recognize Pell\'s line as a lesser seat',fx:'g rel:ret_s loy 6; o priest loy -8; ?x claim 10',d:[6,11,'claim3']},
{l:'Declare the teaching false',fx:'o priest loy 5; g rel:ret_s grv 8',d:[6,11,'claim3']},
{l:'Debate Pell\'s followers yourself',fx:'r cha 4',ch:[[.6,'g all bel 4','You answer what only you could know. The grey delegation leaves quieter.'],[.4,'r cha -6; g all bel -3','They ask about a day you do not remember.']]}]},
{id:'claim3',t:'Two Seats',fu:1,who:'The council, alarmed',
x:`The grey seat has outlived Pell. There is now a second child, found by a second Search, with a second treasury. Foreign envoys call on both courts. The council asks you to end it before your next death, when there will be no one to say which is which.`,
q:`"One of you must be the copy. Settle it while you can still speak."`,
ch:[{l:'Merge the seats: adopt the child',fx:'r leg 4; o priest loy -5; g rel:ret_s loy 6; x claim -8'},
{l:'Outlaw the grey seat',fx:'r ord -2; o priest loy 6; g rel:ret_s grv 8; m rel:ret_s -10 p the outlawing of the grey seat; x claim -12'},
{l:'Let both stand',fx:'r cha -3; g all loy 2; ?x claim 12'}]},
/* ---- Chain 11: the grove ---- */
{id:'tuun1',t:'The Grey Alders',era:[1,2],w:20,who:'Old Aino of the Tuun',
x:`Your builders want the grey alders at the forest edge for hall beams. Old Aino has walked out of the Tuunwood to ask that they stand. The alders, she says, are where the Tuun dead are. She has brought honey and no warriors.`,
q:`"You have died and come back. You know the dead need somewhere to be."`,
ch:[{l:'Cut the alders',fx:'r tre 10; r ord 2; v moot att -15; m eth:tu -14 p the cutting of the grey alders',d:[5,10,'tuun2'],f:'alders_cut'},
{l:'Trade for timber from deeper in',fx:'r tre -3; v moot att 8; r kno 1'},
{l:'Swear the grove inviolate for all your lives',fx:'r tre -4; o merch loy -4; o noble loy -3; v moot att 15; m eth:tu 14 p the Grove Oath',d:[5,10,'tuun2'],f:'grove_oath'}]},
{id:'tuun2',t:'The Forest Remembers',fu:1,who:'Aino\'s {kin}',
x:`{?grove_oath:Fever is in the Vale. Aino's {kin} comes with bark and moss that break it, and asks nothing, because of the Grove Oath of your {srcOrd} life.|Timber carts are being ambushed on the forest road. Aino's {kin} sends word: the alders were cut in your {srcOrd} life, and the dead have nowhere to be but the road.}`,
q:`{?grove_oath:"Will you send your sick to us, into the forest?"|"Will you make it right?"}`,
ch:[{l:'{?grove_oath:Send the sick to the Tuun|Replant the grove and pay a wergild}',fx:'{?grove_oath:r food 4; g all loy 2; v moot att 5; o priest loy -8|r tre -12; v moot att 12; m eth:tu 8 t the replanting of the alders}',d:[6,11,'tuun3']},
{l:'{?grove_oath:Accept the medicine, keep your people home|Send the war band up the road}',fx:'{?grove_oath:r food 3; o priest loy 4|r ord 5; r tre 4; o army loy 3; v moot att -12; g eth:tu grv 10}'},
{l:'Ask the Tuun to swear to the realm',fx:'v moot att -4; g eth:tu loy 4',d:[6,11,'tuun3']}]},
{id:'tuun3',t:'Charcoal',fu:1,who:'A master of the forges',
x:`The forges eat charcoal faster than the open woods can give it. The forge-masters want the alder groves. {?grove_oath:The Grove Oath of year {srcRootYear} stands in the way.|The replanted grove stands in the way.} They point out that the Tuun do not vote, pay or fight for you, and iron does all three.`,
q:`"An oath to the dead, or bread for the living?"`,
ch:[{l:'Open the groves to the forges',fx:'r tre 10; r kno 4; o merch loy 6; v moot att -20; m eth:tu -20 p the breaking of the Grove Oath'},
{l:'The groves stand',fx:'o merch loy -6; r kno -2; v moot att 8; g eth:tu loy 6'},
{l:'Shared forestry under Tuun wardens',fx:'r tre 3; v moot att 6; o merch loy -2; g eth:tu loy 4'}]},
/* ---- Chain 12: the press ---- */
{id:'press1',t:'Joska\'s Press',era:[3,4],w:16,c:{tech:['press']},who:'Joska, a printer',
x:`Joska wants to print your sayings in the common tongues, cheap, without the Keepers' commentary around them. People would read you directly for the first time. The Temple has always been the only door to your words.`,
q:`"They are your words. Whose are they to sell?"`,
ch:[{l:'License the printing freely',fx:'r kno 5; r cha 4; g all bel 3; o priest loy -10; o priest aut -6',d:[5,10,'press2']},
{l:'Print only under the Temple\'s seal',fx:'o priest loy 6; o priest aut 6; r kno 2'},
{l:'Print in Kaldic only',fx:'r kno 3; o priest loy -4; g lang:kal loy 3',d:[5,10,'press2']}]},
{id:'press2',t:'An Office or a Soul',fu:1,who:'A pamphlet, read aloud by your steward',
x:`A pamphlet asks whether "the Returner" is a soul at all, or an office that the realm fills with a convenient child and a story. It is well argued. It quotes your own printed sayings. It has sold in every market town.`,
q:`"Shall I find the author, or a better pamphleteer?"`,
ch:[{l:'Seize the pamphlets',fx:'r ord 2; g cls:artisan grv 8; g cls:merchant grv 5; r kno -3'},
{l:'Answer it publicly from memory',fx:'r cha 3',ch:[[.5,'g all bel 5','You recount what no office could know.'],[.5,'g all bel -6; r cha -3','Your answer is printed too, with annotations.']],d:[5,10,'press3']},
{l:'Say nothing',fx:'g all bel -3; r leg 3'}]},
{id:'press3',t:'The Academy\'s Proposal',fu:1,who:'The Rector of the Academy',
x:`The Academy proposes to examine you: sealed questions about your past lives, checked against sealed archives, results published. If you pass, doubt becomes unfashionable. If you fail, it becomes a science.`,
q:`"You have nothing to fear from measurement. Have you?"`,
ch:[{l:'Submit to the examination',fx:'o school pow 5',ch:[[.65,'r cha 10; g all bel 8; r leg 4; x recog 8','You pass. The report runs to nine volumes.'],[.35,'r cha -12; g all bel -8','The report notes "discrepancies".']]},
{l:'Refuse: faith is not a laboratory',fx:'r cha 3; o priest loy 7; o school loy -6; g cls:artisan bel -3'},
{l:'Make the examination the law of recognition',fx:'law recog trial; o school pow 8; r kno 4; o priest loy -8; r leg 6'}]},
/* ---- Chain 13: the charter ---- */
{id:'pact1',t:'The Charter',era:[1,2,3],w:16,pick:'newReg',who:'The assembly of {rn}',
x:`The notables of {rn} offer their loyalty in writing, on terms: their own judges, their own tongue in their courts, their levies commanded by their own. In exchange they will never again ask whose land it is.`,
q:`"We can be your subjects or your allies. Allies are cheaper."`,
ch:[{l:'Grant the charter',fx:'fed $r 1; g $g loy 10; reg $r unrest -12; g core loy -4; m $g 12 p the Charter of {rn}',d:[5,10,'pact2'],f:'charter'},
{l:'Refuse: one law for all',fx:'g $g grv 6; reg $r unrest 6; r leg 5; g core loy 4; reg $r integ 4'},
{l:'Grant it to their notables only',fx:'g $g+cls:noble loy 8; g $g+cls:merchant loy 6; g $g grv 3; reg $r integ 5'}]},
{id:'pact2',t:'The Levy Withheld',fu:1,who:'Your marshal',
x:`You have called the levies. {rn} has sent a letter instead: under the Charter of your {srcOrd} life its men are commanded by their own, and their own have decided this is not their war.`,
q:`"A charter is a promise. So is an army. Which do you keep?"`,
ch:[{l:'Honour the charter',fx:'o army loy -5; g $g loy 7; r leg 4; r ord -2',d:[5,10,'pact3']},
{l:'March the levy out by force',fx:'fed $r 0; o army loy 7; o army pow 4; r ord 3; g core loy 3; g $g grv 12; m $g -16 p the breaking of the Charter of {rn}; reg $r unrest 12'},
{l:'Accept silver in place of men',fx:'r tre 5; o army loy -6; g $g w -3',d:[5,10,'pact3']}]},
{id:'pact3',t:'Charters for All',fu:1,who:'Delegates of three lands',
x:`{rn} has prospered under its charter, and the other lands have noticed. Delegates of three lands ask for the same: every land its own charter, and a written compact above them all, binding even you.`,
q:`"You gave it to one. Was that justice or favour?"`,
ch:[{l:'A compact of chartered lands',fx:'law gov federal; r leg 8; g all loy 3; g core loy -6; o council loy -6'},
{l:'One charter was favour enough',fx:'g all grv 4; o council loy 4'},
{l:'Revoke the first charter instead',fx:'r tre 5; o council loy 6; g core loy 5; fed $r 0; law gov direct; g $g grv 14; m $g -18 p the revoking of the Charter of {rn}; r leg -4'}]},
/* ---- Standalone, era 1 ---- */
{id:'drought',t:'The Dry Summer',era:[1],w:14,who:'The keeper of the granary',
x:`The summer rains failed. There is grain for the Vale or seed for next year, and the war band eats first by custom. The Hill clans have already driven their herds to your wells.`,
q:`"Three mouths and two loaves. Who eats?"`,
ch:[{l:'Feed the war band first',fx:'o army loy 10; r food -4; g cls:farmer grv 8; g eth:kh grv 6'},
{l:'Equal shares, the band included',fx:'o army loy -6; r food -6; g all loy 3'},
{l:'Open the wells and granary to the Hill clans',fx:'r food -10; g eth:kh loy 8; m eth:kh 8 t the open wells in the dry summer; g eth:kr grv 5'},
{l:'Save the seed; let this year be hungry',fx:'r food 4; g all grv 6; r ord -4'}]},
{id:'tribute',t:'The Khan\'s Tenth',era:[1,2],w:14,c:{max:{'v.horde.att':60}},who:'A Sorvek envoy, mounted in your hall',
x:`The Sorvek khan asks a tenth of your herds each autumn. In return his riders will pass your pastures by. His envoy does not dismount to say it. Your captains count his escort and say nothing.`,
q:`"The grass belongs to those who can cross it. A tenth, or all?"`,
ch:[{l:'Pay the tenth',fx:'r food -6; v horde att 10; o army loy -6; r cha -3'},
{l:'Refuse and fortify the fords',fx:'r tre -5; v horde att -8; o army loy 7; r cha 3',ch:[[.35,'r food -8; reg hk unrest 8','They come anyway, and take more than a tenth.']]},
{l:'Offer a marriage between the lines',fx:'v horde att 12; g eth:kr loy -3; ?c army sv 6',pv:'Kin bring kin.'}]},
{id:'feast',t:'The Seat at Your Right',era:[1],w:12,who:'Your steward',
x:`At the midwinter feast one person sits at your right hand, and the whole Vale reads the year's weather in who it is. The clan heads expect it. The Hill chief has ridden three days hoping for it. Mother Senna says nothing, loudly.`,
q:`"The benches are filling. Whom do I seat beside you?"`,
ch:[{l:'The eldest clan head',fx:'o noble loy 6; r tra 3; o priest loy -3'},
{l:'The Hill chief',fx:'g eth:kh loy 8; reg hk integ 5; o noble loy -5'},
{l:'Mother Senna',fx:'o priest loy 8; o priest pow 3; g rel:ret_s bel 4; o noble loy -3'},
{l:'A herder chosen by lot',fx:'r cha 4; g cls:herder loy 5; o noble loy -6; r tra -2'}]},
{id:'healer',t:'The Murrain',era:[1,2],w:12,adv:1,who:'A frightened herder',
x:`Cattle are dying in the upper Vale with black tongues. The herders blame Marta, a healer of the old rites, who was seen walking the pens at night. Your advisors disagree whether this is a curse, a sickness that spreads by touch, or a feud wearing a mask.`,
q:`"Give us Marta, or give us a reason."`,
ch:[{l:'Hand Marta to the herders',fx:'g cls:herder loy 6; g rel:anc grv 8; m rel:anc -8 t the death of Marta the healer',ch:[[.6,'r food -8','The cattle keep dying.']]},
{l:'Pen the sick herds apart and burn the dead',fx:'r food -4; g cls:herder grv 6',ch:[[.7,'r food 6; r kno 2','The dying stops within a month.']]},
{l:'Have Marta treat the herds under guard',fx:'o priest loy -4',ch:[[.5,'r food 4; g rel:anc loy 6','Her poultices work.'],[.5,'r food -6; r cha -3','They do not.']]}]},
{id:'dreamer',t:'The Other Dreamer',era:[1],w:12,who:'Orlen, a shaman of the old rites',
x:`Orlen of the ancestor rites says before the clans that your memories are stolen dreams, and that any ghost-ridden fool can claim a dead man's name. He challenges you to name what lies buried under the hearthstone of the old long-hall. He seems very sure.`,
q:`"If you were here before, say what is under the stone."`,
ch:[{l:'Answer the challenge',fx:'',ch:[[.7,'r cha 8; g rel:anc bel 8; g all bel 3','You name it. They lift the stone. It is there.'],[.3,'r cha -8; g all bel -5','You name it. They lift the stone. Someone has been there first.']]},
{l:'"I do not perform." Refuse',fx:'r cha -2; g rel:anc bel -4; r tra 2'},
{l:'Invite Orlen into your Circle',fx:'o priest loy -6; g rel:anc loy 6; g rel:anc bel 5; c priest kh 4'}]},
{id:'oldbody',t:'The Failing Body',era:[1,2,3,4],w:14,c:{min:{age:45}},who:'Your physician',
x:`Your physician has stopped pretending. This body has some years, and not many. The court can smell it. Those who would rule when you are gone have begun to be polite to each other, which is never a good sign.`,
q:`"Will you name who holds the seat, while your naming still frightens them?"`,
ch:[{l:'Name the Keepers regent, publicly',fx:'x regent priest; o priest loy 6; o army loy -4; o council loy -4'},
{l:'Name the council regent, publicly',fx:'x regent council; o council loy 6; o priest loy -5; r leg 3'},
{l:'Name the marshal regent, publicly',fx:'x regent army; o army loy 8; o priest loy -5; o council loy -4'},
{l:'Name no one. Let them wonder',fx:'r cha 4; o priest loy 2; o council loy 2; o army loy 2; r ord -3'}]},
/* ---- Standalone, era 2 ---- */
{id:'coin',t:'Thin Silver',era:[2,3],w:12,c:{tech:['coinage']},who:'The master of the mint',
x:`The mint-master can stretch the silver: a little copper in every coin, and the treasury fills. Merchants weigh coins. Soldiers and farmers do not, until the merchants stop taking them.`,
q:`"No one will notice for a year. How much do you need this year?"`,
ch:[{l:'Debase the coin',fx:'r tre 14; ?o merch loy -10; ?g cls:artisan grv 8; ?v league att -6',pv:'Merchants weigh coins.'},
{l:'Keep the coin true',fx:'o merch loy 4; v league att 3'},
{l:'Debase only the soldiers\' pay',fx:'r tre 7; ?o army loy -10',pv:'Soldiers spend their pay in markets.'}]},
{id:'marriage',t:'A Wife for the Body',era:[2,3],w:12,who:'Envoys of two courts',
x:`This body is unmarried, and two courts have noticed. The Imeric Crown offers a princess and peace. The League of Sor offers a banker's daughter and credit. Your Keepers observe that the Returner has no heirs, only returns, and that children of the body have confused people before.`,
q:`"A soul may be eternal. A dynasty is at least punctual. Whom will you wed?"`,
ch:[{l:'The Imeric princess',fx:'v crown att 18; v league att -5; g rel:lamp loy 6; o priest loy -6; ?x claim 6',f:'body_heirs'},
{l:'The banker\'s daughter',fx:'v league att 15; r tre 10; o merch pow 5; o noble loy -5',f:'body_heirs'},
{l:'No one. The Returner does not found a house',fx:'o priest loy 6; r cha 3; v crown att -4; v league att -4'}]},
{id:'heirs',t:'The Son of the Last Body',era:[2,3,4],w:18,c:{min:{lives:2},flag:['body_heirs']},who:'A grey-haired man with your old face',
x:`He is older than you now and has your last body's jaw. He is its son. He ruled a province in your name while you were a child, and ruled it well. He kneels, correctly, and asks what a father who is younger than his son owes him.`,
q:`"You remember holding me. Do you remember promising me anything?"`,
ch:[{l:'Confirm him in his province, hereditary',fx:'o noble loy 8; o noble pow 5; r leg -3; ?x claim 6'},
{l:'Thank him and retire him with honour',fx:'r tre -5; o noble loy -4'},
{l:'Bring him onto the council',fx:'o council pow 4; o council loy 4; o priest loy -4'}]},
{id:'plague',t:'Sickness on the Road',era:[2,3],w:12,adv:1,who:'A rider from the south',
x:`A rider reports a coughing death in a caravan town four days south. It may be marsh fever, which passes. It may be the other thing. Closing the roads now costs the autumn trade. Waiting a fortnight will tell you which it is, either way.`,
q:`"Close the roads today, or know more in a fortnight?"`,
ch:[{l:'Close the roads now',fx:'r tre -8; o merch loy -6; v league att -3',ch:[[.5,'g all loy 4; r cha 3','It was the other thing. Your towns are spared.']]},
{l:'Wait for certainty',fx:'',ch:[[.5,'g all size -6; r ord -6; g all grv 6','It was the other thing. It arrives with the certainty.'],[.5,'r tre 3','Marsh fever. The caravans come through.']]},
{l:'Close only the southern road',fx:'r tre -3',ch:[[.25,'g all size -3; r ord -3','It comes around by the river.']]}]},
{id:'quarter',t:'The Soranni Quarter',era:[2,3],w:12,who:'A consul of the League of Sor',
x:`The League asks for a walled quarter in your river port where Soranni traders live under Soranni judges and pay one fixed fee. Trade would treble. Your own judges would stop at its gate.`,
q:`"We bring the sea to your door. We ask only to keep our own house on it."`,
ch:[{l:'Grant the quarter',fx:'r tre 8; v league att 12; o merch pow 5; g eth:so loy 6; r leg -4; ?g eth:kr+cls:artisan grv 8'},
{l:'A quarter, under your judges',fx:'r tre 4; v league att 3'},
{l:'No foreign walls inside ours',fx:'v league att -8; g eth:kr loy 3'}]},
{id:'mission',t:'Lamp-Bearers at the Gate',era:[2,3],w:12,who:'Lamp-Warden Ushet',
x:`Lamp-Warden Ushet of the Imeric Crown asks leave for nine teachers to preach the Nine Lamps in your towns. They heal, they teach letters, they ask no tithe. Your Keepers ask whether you have ever seen a gift from the Crown that stayed a gift.`,
q:`"We light lamps. Does the Returner fear a little light?"`,
ch:[{l:'Let them preach',fx:'v crown att 8; r kno 3; o priest loy -11; ?g rel:lamp size 8'},
{l:'Let them heal and teach, not preach',fx:'v crown att 5; r kno 2; g all loy 1; o priest loy -2'},
{l:'Turn them back at the border',fx:'v crown att -10; o priest loy 6; g rel:lamp grv 6'}]},
{id:'tomb',t:'The Relic Trade',era:[2,3,4],w:14,c:{min:{lives:2}},who:'A pilgrim who paid too much',
x:`Pilgrims crowd the tomb of your last body. The Keepers sell them threads from its shroud. By your count the shroud would now cover the Vale. A pilgrim holds out a thread and asks if it is truly yours.`,
q:`"I sold a cow for this. Tell me it touched you."`,
ch:[{l:'"It did." Bless the trade',fx:'o priest loy 6; o priest aut 5; r tre 4; r cha -3'},
{l:'"It did not." End the trade',fx:'o priest loy -10; o priest aut -6; r cha 5; g all bel 2'},
{l:'Empty the tomb: "I am not in there."',fx:'r cha 6; r tra -6; o priest loy -8; g rel:ret_s bel 6'}]},
/* ---- Standalone, era 3 ---- */
{id:'census',t:'The Great Count',era:[3],w:12,who:'The First Secretary',
x:`The bureaucracy wants to count everyone: by household, and also by tongue and by faith, "for the better apportioning of offices". People who have never had to say what they are will have to choose one box.`,
q:`"We cannot govern what we cannot count. May we ask them what they are?"`,
ch:[{l:'Count by tongue and faith',fx:'r leg 6; r tre 6; o council pow 5; x count 1; ?g all grv 2; ?x cohere 1',pv:'A box, once ticked, is a thing one belongs to.'},
{l:'Count households only',fx:'r leg 2; r tre 2'},
{l:'No count',fx:'o council loy -4; r tra 3; g all loy 2'}]},
{id:'exams',t:'Sons of Examiners',era:[3],w:12,who:'A deputation of senior clerks',
x:`The senior clerks propose that sons of serving officials be excused the first examination, "to preserve the traditions of the service". Nearly all serving officials are of one people. The clerks present this as a coincidence.`,
q:`"Loyalty is learned at a father's desk. Will you reward it?"`,
ch:[{l:'Grant the exemption',fx:'o council loy 8; o council aut 8; ?x close council'},
{l:'Refuse it',fx:'o council loy -6'},
{l:'Refuse, and reserve places for other peoples',fx:'o council loy -10; x open council; g core loy -4'}]},
{id:'general',t:'The Victor\'s Welcome',era:[2,3],w:12,c:{min:{'o.army.pow':40}},who:'The crowd outside',
x:`Your general has come home from the frontier with a victory, a devoted army and a new nickname. The crowd is chanting it. It is not your name. He awaits your pleasure at the gate, in full armour, with eight thousand men.`,
q:`"He asks how you wish to receive him. The men are also curious."`,
ch:[{l:'A triumph, and the marshal\'s staff',fx:'o army loy 8; o army aut 10; o army pow 4; r cha -3'},
{l:'Honours, and a governorship far away',fx:'r tre -5; o army loy -3'},
{l:'Dismiss him and split his command',fx:'o army aut -10; o army loy -12; o army pow -5',ch:[[.25,'r ord -10; o army loy -6','Two regiments refuse the order for a week.']]}]},
{id:'heresy',t:'Can the Returner Err?',era:[2,3],w:12,who:'Two theologians, shouting',
x:`Keepers teach that you are the Return and cannot err in doctrine. Seekers teach that you are a soul learning, and err like any soul. Both cite you. Both are right about what you said. They have come to blows in the Temple court and demand you settle it.`,
q:`"Tell us what you are. One of us is teaching a lie."`,
ch:[{l:'"I do not err." The Keepers are right',fx:'o priest loy 8; o priest aut 5; g rel:ret_s grv 10; r cha 3'},
{l:'"I err and return to mend it." The Seekers are right',fx:'g rel:ret_s loy 8; o priest loy -10; r cha -2; r leg 3'},
{l:'Forbid the question',fx:'r ord 2; o priest loy -3; g rel:ret_s grv 4'}]},
{id:'archive',t:'The Official Lives',era:[3,4],w:14,c:{min:{lives:3}},who:'The Temple historian',
x:`The Temple has compiled the official history of your lives. You read it. It is handsome, and wrong in several places, always in the Temple's favour. The historian knows you know. He also knows the next Search will test claimants against this book.`,
q:`"Memory fades, even yours. Shall the book stand as written?"`,
ch:[{l:'Let it stand',fx:'o priest loy 6; o priest aut 8; ?x claim 8',pv:'The next child will be examined against it.'},
{l:'Correct it line by line',fx:'o priest loy -8; o priest aut -8; x recog 6; r kno 2'},
{l:'Commission a rival history from the schools',fx:'r tre -6; o school pow 5; o priest loy -5; r kno 3; x recog 3'}]},
/* ---- Standalone, era 4 ---- */
{id:'strike',t:'The Mill Stands Still',era:[4],w:14,who:'A weaver, and behind her an owner',
x:`The weavers of the great mill have stopped the looms over a pay cut. They carry your image and quote your words about thresholds. The owners carry the lease you signed and quote your words about oaths. The garrison commander awaits instructions.`,
q:`"We both have your word. Which did you mean?"`,
ch:[{l:'Side with the weavers',fx:'g cls:artisan loy 10; g cls:artisan bel 5; o merch loy -12; r tre -4'},
{l:'Side with the owners',fx:'o merch loy 8; r tre 4; g cls:artisan grv 12; m cls:artisan -10 t the breaking of the mill strike'},
{l:'Impose an arbitration board',fx:'r leg 5; o merch loy -4; g cls:artisan loy 3; o council pow 3'}]},
{id:'nation',t:'The Homeland Gazette',era:[4],w:14,pick:'aggrEth',who:'The censor',
x:`A newspaper in the tongue of the {gn} has begun to use a new word for where they live. It translates as "homeland", and it is not the name of your realm. The editor is careful, lawful and widely read.`,
q:`"There is no law against a word. Do you want one?"`,
ch:[{l:'Close the paper',fx:'r ord 3; g core loy 3; g $g fear 20; g $g grv 10; m $g -12 t the closing of the Homeland Gazette; ?x cohere 1'},
{l:'Invite the editor into the assembly',fx:'g $g loy 8; g core loy -4; r leg 3'},
{l:'Fund a loyal paper in the same tongue',fx:'r tre -6; g $g loy 3',ch:[[.4,'g $g grv 4','Nobody reads it. Everybody knows who pays for it.']]}]},
{id:'vote',t:'The Assembly Bill',era:[4],w:14,who:'The Speaker of the council',
x:`The council proposes an elected assembly to make law, with the Returner as "perpetual guardian of the compact". You would open sessions and bless outcomes. The bill is silent on what happens if you disagree with one.`,
q:`"The realm has outgrown one voice. Will you be its conscience, or its obstacle?"`,
ch:[{l:'Sign it',fx:'r leg 14; g all loy 5; r cha -8; o priest loy -10; o council pow 6'},
{l:'Sign it, with a guardian\'s veto',fx:'r leg 7; g all loy 2; o council loy -5'},
{l:'Refuse',fx:'r cha 6; r tra 3; o priest loy 8; o council loy -8; g cls:artisan grv 6; g cls:merchant grv 4'}]},
{id:'engine',t:'The Reckoning Engine',era:[4],w:14,who:'The Engine\'s chief attendant',
x:`The Academy's reckoning engine has been fed every recorded saying of all your lives. It can now complete your sentences. The attendant asks who should hold its key: the Temple wants it as scripture, the state as an oracle, the scholars as an instrument.`,
q:`"It speaks rather like you. Whom should it answer to?"`,
ch:[{l:'The Temple',fx:'o priest pow 8; o priest loy 6; o school loy -8; x sing 6'},
{l:'The civil service',fx:'o council pow 8; r leg 5; o priest loy -6; x sing 6'},
{l:'The scholars, with open books',fx:'o school pow 8; r kno 6; o priest loy -6; x sing 10'},
{l:'Lock it. One of me is enough',fx:'r cha 3; o school loy -10; r kno -4; x sing -8'}]},
{id:'rail',t:'The First Line',era:[4],w:14,pick:'newReg',who:'The Minister of Works',
x:`There is money for one railway. Through the Vale it serves the people who already have everything. Through {rn} it binds a land that still half belongs elsewhere, and runs past its markets carrying your soldiers as easily as its grain.`,
q:`"Iron goes where you point. Where?"`,
ch:[{l:'Through {rn}',fx:'r tre -10; reg $r integ 15; g $g loy 4; g core grv 4'},
{l:'Through the Vale',fx:'r tre -6; r food 4; g core loy 5; reg $r integ -4'},
{l:'Let the banks build it where it pays',fx:'r tre 4; o merch pow 8; o merch aut 6'}]},
{id:'conscript',t:'Every Man a Soldier',era:[4],w:14,who:'The War Minister',
x:`The War Minister wants every man of twenty to serve two years, of every people, in mixed regiments, drilled in one tongue. It would make an army of the whole realm. It would also teach the whole realm to shoot.`,
q:`"A nation in arms, or an army apart from the nation?"`,
ch:[{l:'Universal service, mixed regiments',fx:'law rec all; o army pow 10; x open army; ?g all grv 3'},
{l:'Keep the professional army',fx:'o army loy 5; o army aut 5'},
{l:'Universal service, regiments by people',fx:'law rec all; o army pow 8; ?x cohere 1',pv:'Regiments that share a tongue share other things.'}]},
/* ---- More standalone ---- */
{id:'bodykin',t:'The Mother of This Body',era:[2,3,4],w:14,c:{min:{lives:2}},who:'The woman who bore this body',
x:`The woman who bore this body has come to court. She is of the {be}, and speaks {bl}. The chamberlain wants to know where she stands at ceremonies. The Keepers say the Returner has no mother. She has not asked for anything. She is just looking at you.`,
q:`"Where shall she stand?"`,
ch:[{l:'Beside the seat',fx:'g birth loy 8; g birth bel 6; o priest loy -9; r tra -4'},
{l:'Among the honoured guests',fx:'g birth loy 5; r tre -2; o priest loy 1'},
{l:'"The Returner has no mother."',fx:'o priest loy 5; r tra 2; g birth loy -6; ?m birth -6 t the mother turned away at court'}]},
{id:'grave',t:'Your Own Bones',era:[1,2,3],w:12,c:{min:{lives:2}},who:'The clan heads',
x:`The clan heads wish to move the bones of your first body to their ancestral mound, "where the founders lie". It would make you an ancestor of their houses. The Keepers would rather the bones stayed in the shrine, where they are an ancestor of nobody but the Temple.`,
q:`"They are your bones. Where do you want to have been buried?"`,
ch:[{l:'The clan mound',fx:'o noble loy 6; r tra 3; o priest loy -7; g rel:anc bel 5'},
{l:'The shrine',fx:'o priest loy 6; o priest pow 3; o noble loy -5'},
{l:'Scatter them in the river',fx:'r cha 7; g rel:ret_s bel 5; r tra -3; o noble loy -3; o priest loy -3'}]},
{id:'tutor',t:'What You Used to Believe',era:[2,3,4],w:12,c:{min:{lives:3}},who:'A veteran of your last life',
x:`An old soldier who served your last body stops you in the yard. You have reversed a judgment that body made, and men died for the first one. He does not accuse you. He asks whether the dead served a mistake, or whether you have changed.`,
q:`"Were you right then, or are you right now?"`,
ch:[{l:'"I was right then. The world changed."',fx:'o army loy 4; r tra 3'},
{l:'"I was wrong then."',fx:'r cha -3; o army loy -5; r leg 3; g all loy 2'},
{l:'"I am not that man. I only remember him."',fx:'r cha 4; r tra -5; o priest loy -5; g rel:ret_s bel 5'}]},
{id:'hillking',t:'A King in the Hills',era:[2,3],w:12,c:{max:{'g.eth:kh.loy':45}},who:'A Hill Kaldar envoy',
x:`A Hill Kaldar chief has begun calling himself King of High Kald. He does not deny you. He says the Returner is the soul of all Kaldar, and a soul does not collect taxes. He offers to remain your most devoted worshipper.`,
q:`"He will kneel to the shaman. He will not kneel to the Vale. Is that enough?"`,
ch:[{l:'Accept: soul of all, king of some',fx:'fed hk 1; g eth:kh loy 10; g eth:kh bel 8; r leg -5; g eth:kr loy -5'},
{l:'March on him',fx:'r tre -6; g eth:kh grv 8; g eth:kr loy 4; m eth:kh -12 p the war on the Hill King',ch:[[.6,'r ord 6; g eth:kh fear 30; o army loy 4; reg hk integ 6','He is taken at the second pass.'],[.4,'o army pow -8; r ord -8','The hills swallow the column.']]},
{l:'Crown him yourself, as your vassal',fx:'g eth:kh loy 6; r tra 3; o noble loy -5; reg hk integ 5'}]}
];
